# Morphe Workspace Rules

Full project context and all specialist agent prompts are in **AGENTS.md** at the repo root.
Read AGENTS.md before doing any substantive work.

## Core Rules

1. **Check state first.** Before acting on any app, check what analysis files exist.
   Never assume pipeline stage.

2. **Never use obfuscated names in fingerprints.** Single-letter class/method names
   (a, b, H) change every app update. Always derive fingerprints from stable smali
   characteristics (SDK calls, string literals, access flags, return types).

3. **Verify against smali, not jadx.** jadx can decompile incorrectly. The smali is
   always the ground truth.

4. **Never push without approval.** All git commits and pushes require explicit user OK.

5. **Always use original APK.** CLI patching always uses the file in `analysis/<app>/apk/`.
   Never use `base.apk` or extracted splits as CLI input.

## Pipeline State Check

```bash
ls analysis/<app>/notes/recon.md analysis/<app>/decompiled/ analysis/<app>/smali/ \
   paresh-patches/patches/src/main/kotlin/app/paresh/patches/<app>/ 2>/dev/null
```

## Patch Structure

```
paresh-patches/patches/src/main/kotlin/app/paresh/patches/<app>/
├── shared/Constants.kt
└── <category>/
    ├── Fingerprints.kt
    └── <Name>Patch.kt
```

## Quick Commands

```bash
cd paresh-patches && ./gradlew buildAndroid
VER=$(grep "^version" paresh-patches/gradle.properties | cut -d= -f2 | tr -d ' ')
java -jar morphe-cli.jar list-patches -p "paresh-patches/patches/build/libs/patches-${VER}.mpp" -pvo
```
